{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792609566,"nonce":"q+NnLbNVeRw4/TBVhorCCHzg+KU=","title":"TypeScript: migrate the conformance oracle to 7.1","message":"The reference harness currently pins TypeScript 6.0.2 and relies on the legacy monolithic compiler API. TypeScript 7.1.0-beta is published as of 2026-10-20, with a native Go-backed compiler and a new sync/async compiler API. Update the oracle adapter and exact dependency lock, regenerate reference results with the actual 7.1 checker/emitter, and retain diagnostic categories, relative multi-file resolution, Node runtime output, source/options/version validation and honest failure reporting. Centralize the version pin rather than repeating a hard-coded compiler version across three languages.\n\nAcceptance: live TypeScript 7.1/Node comparisons for the whole local suite, native pinned comparisons across interpreter/Cranelift/LLVM, harness tests including version/failure behavior, and CI installation through the locked package. Existing 6.0.2 results must not be relabeled without running the new checker. Official upstream corpus CI integration remains separate from this oracle migration.","files":null}]}